* text=auto eol=lf
*.zip binary

# Each results/run-*/SHA256SUMS seals its run folder by the SHA-256 of exact bytes.
# `* text=auto eol=lf` above writes LF on checkout, but it still converts line
# endings on commit, and that is how two files in run-2026-10-02-linux were
# committed as LF after being sealed as CRLF. `-text` turns conversion off for the
# sealed folders in both directions, so the committed blob is the sealed bytes and
# checkout writes it unchanged under any core.autocrlf setting. Later lines win.
results/** -text
